ld/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-49244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{5}^{2}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4$, calculate\n${\\int }_{2}^{5}(2f(x)+3)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-49244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{5}^{2}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}(2f(x)+3)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{2}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(4)+3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & =8+3(5-2) \\\\  & =8+3\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-49244" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-49244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-49244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-17"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "13"] ["math" "17"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-49244" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "17"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-7,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(7)\\,-\\,x\\,{|}_{1}^{6} \\\\  & =14\\,-\\,(6-1) \\\\  & =14\\,-\\,5 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346051" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}(f(x)-5)\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{2}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(f(x)-5)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-5\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =1-5(2-0) \\\\  & =1-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-114015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3,$ calculate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(2f(x)+x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(3)\\,+\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{16-1}{2} \\\\  & =6\\,+\\,\\frac{15}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346057" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{27}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}(7-5f(x))\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{4}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}(7-5f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =7{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}x-5{\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\cdot x\\,{|}_{2}^{4}-5\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =7(4-2)+20 \\\\  & =7\\cdot 2+20 \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114017" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-114017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-18"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "34"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114017" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "34"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-316099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8,$ \nthen what is ${\\int }_{1}^{7}(2-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{7}(2-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-316099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{4}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n(-3)+8\\,=\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{7}(2-3f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{7}1\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,3{\\int }_{1}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot x{|}_{1}^{7}\\,-\\,3(5) \\\\  & =2(7-1)-15 \\\\  & =12-15 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-316099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-316099" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-316099" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ then what is ${\\int }_{3}^{6}(5-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8+4 & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 12 & ={\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{6}(5-2f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{3}^{6}\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\cdot x\\,{|}_{3}^{6}-2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =5(6-3)-24 \\\\  & =5(3)-24 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "-9"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114135" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2$ and ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=3,$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2+3 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 1 & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(f(x)+2)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1+2\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =1+2(3-0) \\\\  & =1+6 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=2$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-5$ then what is ${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)+4)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)+4)\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n2+(-5)={\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{6}(2f(x)+4)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{1}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{1}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(-3)+4\\cdot x\\,{|}_{1}^{6} \\\\  & =-6+4(6-1) \\\\  & =-6+20 \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346188" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-346188" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346188" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=7$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$ then what is ${\\int }_{0}^{8}(3+f(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{8}(3+f(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7+1={\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3+f(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot x\\,{|}_{0}^{8}+8 \\\\  & =3(8-0)+8 \\\\  & =24+8 \\\\  & =32\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-346189" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346189" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "32"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{8}^{5}3f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-2$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{3}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{8}^{5}3f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ 3{\\int }_{8}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ -3{\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2 \\\\ {\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{5}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3+\\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{11}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{7}{3}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-114143" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{7}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4,\\,\\,{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{2}{3}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6,$ and ${\\int }_{-1}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=-20.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}\\frac{2}{3}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =6 \\\\ {\\int }_{-3}^{3}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the adjacent intervals rule and substituting known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the sum rule for definite integrals,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{-3}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-3}^{3}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}(-4)-4(9) \\\\  & =-46.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =-46-{\\int }_{-1}^{3}(\\frac{5}{2}f(x)-4g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-46-(-20) \\\\  & =-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346226" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-346226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346226" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-26"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{3}^{0}\\frac{1}{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-1$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=6.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{0}\\frac{1}{3}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{3}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3+6 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4790" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-4790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4790" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $g(x)$ is a  function such that  ${\\int }_{4}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5$ and ${\\int }_{4}^{1}3g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-6.$  What is the value of ${\\int }_{1}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{1}3g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 \\\\ 3{\\int }_{4}^{1}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 \\\\ -3{\\int }_{1}^{4}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-6 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{4}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{4}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+5 \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-4796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "10"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "7"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-4796" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $f$ and $g$ be continuous functions such that ${\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=9,\\,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4,$ and ${\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=10.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}\\frac{1}{2}\\,g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-4 \\\\ {\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the adjacent intervals rule and substituting known values, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy the sum rule for definite integrals,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{8}g(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(9)+(-8) \\\\  & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x & =19-{\\int }_{3}^{8}(3f(x)+g(x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =19-10 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e0366f23d3812e03904accf1acab42f1872d82ef69e7c77814658267bfe22812"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "q-346225" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/state.json" "file_sha256" "c05e4f4d8115a2c96a3add8f2272185f252bbab3d3040011a7e735b84078939c"} {"question" "e-418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_\\pi^\\pi \\sqrt{\\sin x}\\,\\textrm d x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-418.json" "file_sha256" "097303f235af4dfbf5940399479498782725edcfe25362e03a335263c8046964"} {"question" "e-418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the lower and upper limits are the same. So, the integral evaluates to zero:\n\n$$\n\\int_\\pi^\\pi \\sqrt{\\sin x}\\,\\textrm d x = 0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-418.json" "file_sha256" "097303f235af4dfbf5940399479498782725edcfe25362e03a335263c8046964"} {"question" "e-419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{6} \\, f(x) \\; \\textrm d x = -54 },$ what is the value of\n${\\displaystyle \\int_{6}^{0} \\bigg( \\dfrac 1 3 f(x) + 1 \\bigg) \\; \\textrm d x }?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-419.json" "file_sha256" "fe168f882e5a059aa3206f5829677a51982f686e27d37d3d40c67f24d763e637"} {"question" "e-419" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{6}^{0}(\\frac{1}{3}f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{6}^{0}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{6}^{0}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 54+x\\,{|}_{6}^{0} \\\\  & =18+(0-6) \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-419.json" "file_sha256" "fe168f882e5a059aa3206f5829677a51982f686e27d37d3d40c67f24d763e637"} {"question" "e-420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = 18$ and $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = -6$ then what is $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{10} \\big( 2f(x)+1 \\big) \\,\\textrm d x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-420.json" "file_sha256" "aff1d27d896ae722ca35f75eac66fb135da04324c16c564bda461b495f9b7e97"} {"question" "e-420" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x + \\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = \\displaystyle \\int_0^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6+18={\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 12={\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{10}(2f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{0}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{10}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2(12)+x\\,{|}_{0}^{10} \\\\  & =24+(10-0) \\\\  & =34.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-420.json" "file_sha256" "aff1d27d896ae722ca35f75eac66fb135da04324c16c564bda461b495f9b7e97"} {"question" "e-421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\displaystyle \\int_4^1 2 \\, f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = -1}$ \nand ${\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{-1} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 2}.$  What is the value of ${\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^4 f(x) \\, \\textrm dx}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-421.json" "file_sha256" "cf98b0a8b5b4b5181da2ccb5ba6bec4aa73b1a2327794f9664a5e0603683945f"} {"question" "e-421" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's simplify the first given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{4}^{1}2\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ 2{\\int }_{4}^{1}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ -2{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{4}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second integral can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ -{\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004887/example-421.json" "file_sha256" "cf98b0a8b5b4b5181da2ccb5ba6bec4aa73b1a2327794f9664a5e0603683945f"}] "usage" {"e-419" [] "e-420" [] "e-421" [] "e-418" [] "q-49244" []} "basis" 1105 "retractions" [[17592186078951 :question/problem "Given that $∫_{5}^{2}f(x)dx =-4$, calculate\n\n$∫_{2}^{5}(2f(x) + 3)dx$."] [17592186078213 :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int_\\pi^\\pi \\sqrt{\\sin x}\\,\\textrm d x$."] [17592186078214 :question/problem "Given that ${\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{6} \\, f(x) \\; \\textrm d x = -54}$, what is the value of\n${\\displaystyle \\int_{6}^{0} \\bigg(\\dfrac 1 3 f(x) + 1 \\bigg) \\; \\textrm d x}$?"] [17592186078214 :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n∫_{6}^{0}f(x)dx = - ∫_{0}^{6}f(x)dx = 54\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{6}^{0}(\\frac{1}{3}f(x) + 1)dx &= \\frac{1}{3}∫_{6}^{0}f(x)dx + ∫_{6}^{0}1dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 54 + x \\mid _{6}^{0} \\\\\n&= 18 + (0 - 6) \\\\\n&= 12\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078218 :question/problem "If $\\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = 18$ and $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = -6$ then what is $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{10} \\big(2f(x)+1 \\big) \\,\\textrm d x$?"] [17592186078218 :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n\\int_0^{7}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x + \\displaystyle \\int_7^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x = \\displaystyle \\int_0^{10}f(x)\\,\\textrm d x\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information into the above gives the following:\n\n$$\n-6 + 18 = ∫_{0}^{10}f(x)dx; 12 = ∫_{0}^{10}f(x)dx\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the desired integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{0}^{10}(2f(x) + 1)dx &= 2∫_{0}^{10}f(x)dx + ∫_{0}^{10}dx \\\\\n&= 2(12) + x \\mid _{0}^{10} \\\\\n&= 24 + (10 - 0) \\\\\n&= 34\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186078227 :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\displaystyle \\int_4^1 2 \\, f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = -1}$\nand ${\\displaystyle \\int_{1}^{-1} f(x) \\, \\textrm dx = 2}$. What is the value of ${\\displaystyle \\int_{-1}^4 f(x) \\, \\textrm dx}$?"] [17592186078227 :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the first given integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{4}^{1}2f(x)dx &= -1 \\\\\n2∫_{4}^{1}f(x)dx &= -1 \\\\\n- 2∫_{1}^{4}f(x)dx &= -1 \\\\\n∫_{1}^{4}f(x)dx &= \\frac{1}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second integral can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{-1}f(x)dx &= 2 \\\\\n- ∫_{-1}^{1}f(x)dx &= 2 \\\\\n∫_{-1}^{1}f(x)dx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{-1}^{4}f(x)dx &= ∫_{-1}^{1}f(x)dx + ∫_{1}^{4}f(x)dx \\\\\n&=-2 + \\frac{1}{2} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186076918 17592186076919 17592186076920 17592186076921 17592186076922] "immutable_fields" [[17592186076917 :answer-field/correct] [17592186076917 :answer-field/id] [17592186076917 :answer-field/key] [17592186076917 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
